  "title": "skypeek: upcoming asteroid close approaches"
 },
 "description": "skypeek: List asteroid and comet close approaches to Earth. For space weather use get_space_weather. Returns near-Earth object close approaches to Earth in the next 1-30 days within a miss distance (default 0.05 au, about 19.5 lunar distances): designation, approach time, nominal distance with its 3-sigma range, relative velocity, absolute magnitude and diameter (published or a rough range). Data: NASA/JPL Solar System Dynamics close-approach API (US Government work); no endorsement by NASA or JPL is implied. At most 100 approaches per answer. Not an impact-risk assessment. Cached up to an hour. An upstream outage is a 503 upstream_unavailable (not charged). Typically under 1 s. Price: USD 0.001. Free: 5 skypeek calls per IP per UTC day. Docs: https://tanod.dev/learn/asteroid-close-approach-api.html",
 "inputSchema": {
  "properties": {
   "days": {
    "default": 7,
    "description": "Look-ahead window in days (1-30).",
    "maximum": 30,
    "minimum": 1,
    "title": "Days",
    "type": "integer"
   },
   "dist_max_au": {
    "default": 0.05,
    "description": "Largest nominal miss distance in au (0.0001-0.2; 0.05 au is about 19.5 lunar distances).",
    "maximum": 0.2,
    "minimum": 0.0001,
    "title": "Dist Max Au",
    "type": "number"
   }
  },
